  "changes": [
    "Bash runs in native's command shape: eval in an && list, stdin /dev/null, extglob off (bash), merged streams, cwd file on success",
    "commands use the user's bash or zsh with a login-shell snapshot generated by native's steps (rc, shopt, functions, set -o, aliases, PATH)",
    "the shell directory persists inside the project and resets outside with native's message; background commands never move it",
    "native's Bash environment: CLAUDECODE, CLAUDE_CODE_CHILD_SESSION, CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ATTENDED, CLAUDE_CODE_ENTRYPOINT, COREPACK_ENABLE_AUTO_PIN, GIT_EDITOR, SHELL, AI_AGENT, CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID, CLAUDE_EFFORT",
    "results trimmed with native's empty placeholder; failures as 'Exit code N' with native's 30,000 cap and 5,000 head/tail; outputs over 30,000 characters persisted to a private target file with native's preview",
    "output collection drains a closed process (previously large outputs of fast commands were cut at the first read without a marker); hook output is drained the same way",
    "a timed-out command's handle reads its output from the start, as native's output file does; a still-running command's directory file is removed when it ends",
    "hook input carries effort once native reports it; guidance no longer calls project hooks unavailable"
  ],
  "gates": {
    "source_tests": 162,
    "check_compact": "passed on dd1a2367's tree; origin/main merge added only documentation",
    "native_review": "4 read-only Codex review rounds; findings fixed (timeout output, persisted cap, zsh shopt, cwd file lifetime, '..name' directories, reset after persisted preview); the last reported none",
    "acceptance_harness": "packaged acceptance compares 36 Bash cases with tools/claude_shell_native_baseline.json (reproduced exactly by tools/claude_shell_native_probe.py); the split-UTF-8 stream check now requires native's merged result; hook checks read the result's own message and wait for in-flight child hooks (both were order-dependent with a background child)"
  },
